  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "If \\(2x-3y-z=0\\) and \\(x+3y-14z=0,\\) \\(z\\ne0,\\) the numerical value of \\(\\dfrac{x^2+3xy}{y^2+z^2}\\) is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(7\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(0\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(-\\dfrac{20}{17}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(-2\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "a",
    "value": "7"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1964-p19.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Solving the equations gives \\(y=3z\\) and \\(x=5z.\\) Therefore \\[\\frac{x^2+3xy}{y^2+z^2}=\\frac{25z^2+45z^2}{9z^2+z^2}=7.\\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Solve both linear equations for \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) in terms of \\(z\\)",
        "The equations give \\(y=3z\\) and \\(x=5z\\)"
      ],
